s of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{3}+1)^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{5}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{u}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{u}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{-3/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{a}^{3}}}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292546 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292547 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292548 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292549 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292550 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1041 "selection" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292548 13194139534509 true] [17592186292545 1110 #uuid "1c41a572-1358-5776-afe2-d497131fa388" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292546 1034 "The integral diverges" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292546 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534509 true] [17592186292546 1111 #uuid "28e28573-5dd7-5891-995b-6c3e5dfd78d0" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292547 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292547 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534509 true] [17592186292547 1111 #uuid "5053871c