t{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}3{u}^{-5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{3}{4}{u}^{-4}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-4}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{4}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{4}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292553 13194139534509 true] [17592186292552 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292554 13194139534509 true] [17592186292552 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534509 true] [17592186292552 1041 "field-1" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292552 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292554 13194139534509 true] [17592186292552 1110 #uuid "2687e102-dbc8-5a47-83cf-a7c46cd972ca" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292553 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292553 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534509 true] [17592186292553 1111 #uuid "d82a8af2-a9d2-5893-9473-6c317042b707" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292554 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292554 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534509 true] [17592186292554 1111 #uuid "470f44d2-9390-5f11-b444-dd05fbe28bf3" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292555 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292556 13194139534509 true] [17592186292555 1089 "q-350543" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292555 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534509 true] [17592186292555 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{12}{(5\\theta -1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta =$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292555 1113 #uuid "41c4f6a7-69db-5812-9f0a-6a2ff4b7b713" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292555 1145 "First, we substitute $u=5\\theta -1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}\\theta }=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=5\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to -\\infty $ when $\\theta \\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=5\\theta -1$ is as follows:\n\n| $\\theta $ | $-\\infty $ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\infty $ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{0}\\frac{12}{(5\\theta -1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{12}{5{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the lower bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to -\\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{12}{5{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u & =\\frac{12}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{\\int }_{a}^{-1}{u}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}{lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[-{u}^{-1}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }{[\\frac{1}{u}]}_{a}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to -\\infty }[\\frac{1}{(-1)}-\\frac{1}{a}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{5}\\cdot (-1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292556 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292557 13194139534509 true] [17592186292556 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534509 true] [17592186292556 1041 "field-1" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292556 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292557 13194139534509 true] [17592186292556 1110 #uuid "2ed6de76-499a-535b-8349-07e4cb8e1e06" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292557 1034 "\\frac{12}{5}" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292557 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534509 true] [17592186292557 1111 #uuid "95a5be23-15ec-5717-b0bb-c93855685dfb" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292558 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292559 13194139534509 true] [17592186292558 1089 "q-80347" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292558 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534509 true] [17592186292558 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292558 1113 #uuid "9b00f298-c8ee-513b-9db1-ba9601a75ae2" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292558 1145 "First, we substitute $u=8-{x}^{3}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u={x}^{2}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to -\\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=8-{x}^{3}$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & -1 & -\\infty  \\\\ u & 9 & \\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\infty }^{9}(-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{u}})\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{9}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{8-{x}^{3}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{9}^{a}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[2\\sqrt{u}]}_{9}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\sqrt{a}-\\sqrt{9}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\infty  \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent." 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292560 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292561 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292562 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292563 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292564 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1041 "selection" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292561 13194139534509 true] [17592186292559 1110 #uuid "9100afc8-dba2-5771-9b67-77e4a9c47211" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292560 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534509 true] [17592186292560 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534509 true] [17592186292560 1111 #uuid "beed96ca-eee6-57f1-9425-964fba906eb2" 13194139534509 true] [175921